UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 3, Week 38, Lesson 1: Reading and interpreting graphs', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Interpreting graphs means answering questions about most/least, totals, differences and simple conclusions supported by the data.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same method to a larger number or a new context, then compare two solution paths for accuracy.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nFrom a column graph: which is least? What is the difference between top two? About how many in total?\n\nFEEDBACK\nLeast = shortest column; difference = subtract frequencies; total = sum.\n\nWATCH FOR\nSaying “most people like X” when the sample is only your table group overgeneralises.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nAnswer twelve interpretation questions on two graphs. For three answers write the exact numbers you used. Write one careful conclusion that does not overclaim.\n\nWrite a short reflection naming one step you corrected and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"Mathematics","learning_intention":"Interpreting graphs means answering questions about most/least, totals, differences and simple conclusions supported by the data.","lesson_number":1,"lesson_role":"Concept","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil","Optional: place-value chart or number line"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["MA2-DATA-02"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Answer twelve interpretation questions on two graphs. For three answers write the exact numbers you used. Write one careful conclusion that does not overclaim. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Original response on new material: Least = shortest column; difference = subtract frequencies; total = sum. Reasoning: I used interpret by attending to most and explain why it matters rather than copying the worked model.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Common error: Saying “most people like X” when the sample is only your table group overgeneralises. Correction: Least = shortest column; difference = subtract frequencies; total = sum. Why: the correction restores accurate use of interpret.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Saying “most people like X” when the sample is only your table group overgeneralises. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Solve one fresh problem that uses interpret with different numbers from the worked model. Show working and name the places or values that matter.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Describe one likely mistake with interpret, show corrected working, and say why the correction works.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Require new numbers, visible working and named places/values. / Require a real misconception, corrected working and a method reason..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Least = shortest column; difference = subtract frequencies; total = sum. This matches the lesson skill for interpret.","options":["Least = shortest column; difference = subtract frequencies; total = sum.","Saying “most people like X” when the sample is only your table group overgeneralises.","Ignore the task and invent an unrelated answer.","Copy the worked example and call it independent work."],"question":"From a column graph: which is least? What is the difference between top two? About how many in total?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Saying “most people like X” when the sample is only your table group overgeneralises. That misconception weakens accuracy; the other choices align with the lesson idea.","options":["Interpreting graphs means answering questions about most/least, totals, differences and simple conclusions supported by the data.","Least = shortest column; difference = subtract frequencies; total = sum.","Careful use of most and explain why it matters with clear evidence.","Saying “most people like X” when the sample is only your table group overgeneralises."],"question":"Which statement is a common mistake when practising interpret?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Understanding is shown by new evidence and named most and explain why it matters, not by copying the model.","options":["Apply the idea with new evidence and name the most and explain why it matters used.","Repeat the worked example wording with no new evidence.","Choose randomly because any option could be right.","Treat a missing detail as a proven fact."],"question":"A learner is practising interpret. Which approach best shows understanding?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Mathematics answers need labelled working tied to place value or quantity.","options":["Saying “most people like X” when the sample is only your table group overgeneralises.","Show the places, values or steps and say why each step is valid.","Write only a final number with no working.","Change digits to look neater without checking place value."],"question":"Which working note best supports a mathematics answer about interpret?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"The correct statement applies the method; the others break it.","options":["Ignore the task and invent an unrelated answer.","Copy the worked example and call it independent work.","Least = shortest column; difference = subtract frequencies; total = sum.","Saying “most people like X” when the sample is only your table group overgeneralises."],"question":"Using this lesson idea — Interpreting graphs means answering questions about most/least, totals, differences and simple conclusions… — which statement is true?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Disagreement is resolved by checking places, operations and the question focus.","options":["Average the two answers without checking either.","Recheck places, operations and whether the question asked for the quantity you computed.","Pick the longer-looking working automatically.","Delete units so the answers appear to match."],"question":"Which error should you repair first if two methods disagree?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Transfer requires new numbers with the same method.","options":["Change only handwriting and keep the same numbers.","Copy the worked example and call it independent work.","Solve a fresh problem with different numbers and explain the method.","Retype the worked model numbers as the answer."],"question":"Which practice choice shows transfer of interpret?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Useful feedback names the failed step and shows corrected working.","options":["Tell the learner to skip working and only keep the final digits.","Just add more digits until it looks longer.","Name the exact place or step that failed, then show corrected working for interpret.","Praise neat handwriting even when the places are wrong."],"question":"Which feedback comment is most useful after a mistake?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence on new material demonstrates the skill; copying the model does not.","marking_guide":"Require new numbers, visible working and named places/values.","question":"Solve one fresh problem that uses interpret with different numbers from the worked model. Show working and name the places or values that matter.","sample_answer":"Original response on new material: Least = shortest column; difference = subtract frequencies; total = sum. Reasoning: I used interpret by attending to most and explain why it matters rather than copying the worked model.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A useful correction changes the inaccurate idea or method and explains why.","marking_guide":"Require a real misconception, corrected working and a method reason.","question":"Describe one likely mistake with interpret, show corrected working, and say why the correction works.","sample_answer":"Common error: Saying “most people like X” when the sample is only your table group overgeneralises. Correction: Least = shortest column; difference = subtract frequencies; total = sum. Why: the correction restores accurate use of interpret.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent working and reflection, with reasons where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-mat-y3-w38-l1","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA mathematics alignment using verified outcome code wording where recorded in lesson-pipeline/sources; content-point mapping remains pending.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise interpret.","Read the mission before you start calculating.","Keep the place or unit you are working with in view."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your working with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not match the method."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the place or distance that carries the method.","Then write the reason without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore place value or working.","Prefer accurate method over a guess that merely looks neat."],"submit":["Confirm that your working and reason are both present.","Proofread digits, places and operation signs.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title and find the worked model.","Name one exact place, value or distance before you decide.","Try the small prompt before opening the comparison."],"teach1":["Return to the model and list the key numbers.","Say what each number represents in the method.","A final answer alone is weaker than labelled working."],"teach2":["Compare a weak attempt with stronger working.","Change the value or method, not only how neat it looks.","Name the mistake you are repairing."],"teach3":["Choose fresh numbers that still use the same skill.","Write one reason in your own words.","Do not retype the worked model as your answer."],"write":["Follow every part of the independent instructions.","Include original working and a short reason.","Save work that shows the skill on new numbers."]},"subject":"Statistics and Probability","success_criteria":["I can use interpret with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify most and explain why it matters.","I can practise least independently on a new prompt.","I can notice difference needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Interpreting graphs means answering questions about most/least, totals, differences and simple conclusions supported by the data. Supported working follows the actual numbers and purpose of the task. Apply the lesson idea with evidence.","options":["An answer copied without understanding.","A guess with no working.","Interpreting graphs means answering questions about most/least, totals, differences and simple conclusions supported by the data.","A calculation unrelated to the numbers given."],"question":"Which choice best shows accurate use of this idea about interpret?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nIf blue has 12 and red has 7, blue is more popular by 5. Total of all categories answers “how many surveyed” when everyone chose one option.\n\nTRY FIRST\nFrom a column graph: which is least? What is the difference between top two? About how many in total?\n\nFEEDBACK\nLeast = shortest column; difference = subtract frequencies; total = sum.","explain":"Interpreting graphs means answering questions about most/least, totals, differences and simple conclusions supported by the data.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Saying “most people like X” when the sample is only your table group overgeneralises. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Graph interpretation moves.","caption":"Quote numbers in conclusions.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Most / least</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">tallest / shortest</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Difference</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">subtract</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which number or place matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the places, values or distances that carry the method before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":